※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ **A list of the heap's whose room is its own is given back where its scope ends.**  `l` below
※ is made in `⎕heap`, grown where it is and read, and nothing takes its room anywhere else: so
※ where the body ends the room goes back to the heap, by the size its header says, as if
※ `defer` had been written right after the definition.  `once` grows a list of a hundred and
※ twenty-eight words a word at a time and is called two hundred thousand times; a million calls,
※ two gigabytes, ran out of memory at once before, and take longer than the interpreter's tests
※ may.  What counts is the other two: room the size of a class (`reserved`, eight kilobytes a
※ turn, in the slabs) and room mapped on its own (`mapped`, eight hundred kilobytes a turn), each
※ of which would pass what a program run by the tests may have three times over if anything
※ stayed -- so this runs at all only because each list is given back.
※
※ Compare: **Rust**, whose `Vec` is dropped at the end of its scope; **C++**, whose
※ `std::vector` is destroyed there; **Swift**, whose array is released when the last reference
※ goes; **Go**, where the collector finds it some time later; **Zig** and **Odin**, where
※ `defer list.deinit()` is written by hand and forgetting it is a leak.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[opaque]
fn once(n: u64) → u64:
    let l: mut [u64] = [] in ⎕heap
    foreach i: u64 = 0u64…n:
        l ⧺← ⟦i⟧
    ⎕drop(#l)

@[opaque]
fn reserved(n: u64 ¤idx) → u64:
    let l: mut [u64] = []
    ⎕reserve(l, n)
    l ⧺← ⟦⎕drop(n)⟧
    ⎕drop(#l)

@[opaque]
fn mapped(n: u64 ¤idx) → u64:
    let l: mut [u64] = []
    ⎕reserve(l, n)
    l ⧺← ⟦⎕drop(n), ⎕drop(n)⟧
    ⎕drop(#l)

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let total: mut u64 = 0u64
    foreach _: u64 = 0u64…200000u64:
        total ← total + once(128u64)
    if total ≠ 25600000u64:
        return 1u6
    foreach _: u64 = 0u64…200000u64:
        total ← total + reserved(1000)
    if total ≠ 25800000u64:
        return 2u6
    foreach _: u64 = 0u64…2000u64:
        total ← total + mapped(100000)
    if total = 25804000u64: 0u6 else: 3u6
